  "sent_to_model": "yo need a review for the battery backup i got, Kestrel Bastion 1500, for the Voltwise site. it literally saved my ass during the storm last month i had a 10x long open when the power cut. but i want it actually useful for other ppl running trading setups, real numbers not just hype, theres stuff that bugs me about it too. giving it 4 stars. heres what i got\n\n- Kestrel Bastion 1500, 1500VA / 1000W, pure sine wave, paid $229 on Voltwise in Aug 2026\n- my load is PC + 3 monitors + modem + router, around 410W while trading per its own display\n- box says ~14 min at 500W, i got 11 min 40 sec at my load before i shut down, tested it on purpose\n- 10 outlets, 5 battery backed, 5 surge only. USB-C 60W port\n- weighs like 30 lbs, battery is swappable but replacement pack is $95\n- Oct 14 storm, power dropped around 2:20pm, i was 10x long on SOL perp, rig and wifi stayed up, closed it clean in like 4 min\n- first week the fan kicked on at 3am randomly and woke me up, its loud, like a hair dryer on low\n- the desktop app is trash looking, like windows xp, but auto shutdown works which is what matters\n- beeping on outage is loud af, you can mute it in the app but it resets after firmware update\n- plug the modem + router into battery side, ppl forget that and lose internet anyway\n- real numbers for other traders, honest about the annoying stuff, 4 stars\n\n(About me: crypto day-trader, 23, Miami, Florida. Length: it should come to roughly 400-800 words.)",
